IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er4-nouns`
IMPORT `er4-part3-1-premium-reduction`

-- Tests of regs 76.01 to 76.06 (SOR-96-332.txt lines 1177-1208). Every expected value is written by hand from the text.
-- The estimates are invented for the tests; none is a published figure.

§ `Reg 76.01 -- provincial benefits, provincial plan, variable administrative costs`

-- Arguments: paid under a provincial plan, because of pregnancy, care of new-born children, care of children placed for adoption.
#ASSERT `reg 76.01 provincial benefits` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 76.01 provincial benefits` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 76.01 provincial benefits` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.01 provincial benefits` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.01 provincial benefits` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Arguments: established under a provincial law, provides for provincial benefits, agreement with the Government of Canada.
#ASSERT `reg 76.01 provincial plan` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.01 provincial plan` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.01 provincial plan` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.01 provincial plan` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Variable administrative costs: only the direct costs that fluctuate with the number of claims. 100 + 25 counts;
-- 50 (fixed), 30 (not a direct cost of those benefits) do not.
#ASSERT `reg 76.01 variable administrative costs` (LIST (`er4 Operating cost of the Act` OF 100, TRUE, TRUE), (`er4 Operating cost of the Act` OF 50, TRUE, FALSE), (`er4 Operating cost of the Act` OF 30, FALSE, TRUE), (`er4 Operating cost of the Act` OF 25, TRUE, TRUE)) EQUALS 125
#ASSERT `reg 76.01 variable administrative costs` EMPTY EQUALS 0

§ `Reg 76.02 -- the Act and the Regulations are adapted as the Part provides`

#ASSERT `reg 76.02 the Act and these Regulations are adapted for Part III.1 in respect of` `er4 the definition insured participant in section 58 of the Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 76.02 the Act and these Regulations are adapted for Part III.1 in respect of` `er4 subsection 10(13) of the Act, extension of the benefit period` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 76.02 the Act and these Regulations are adapted for Part III.1 in respect of` `er4 paragraph 40(6)(b), the waiting period` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 76.02 the Act and these Regulations are adapted for Part III.1 in respect of` `er4 another provision` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Reg 76.03 -- the standards of a provincial plan`

-- Arguments: day it takes effect, day from which it meets all the requirements, then (a) to (f).
#ASSERT `reg 76.03 the provincial plan meets the requirements from the day it takes effect` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 76.03 the provincial plan meets the requirements from the day it takes effect` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Meeting them only from the day after it takes effect is not "beginning on the day on which it takes effect".
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.03 the provincial plan meets the requirements from the day it takes effect` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 2) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.03 the provincial plan meets the requirements from the day it takes effect` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.03 the provincial plan meets the requirements from the day it takes effect` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.03 the provincial plan meets the requirements from the day it takes effect` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.03 the provincial plan meets the requirements from the day it takes effect` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.03 the provincial plan meets the requirements from the day it takes effect` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.03 the provincial plan meets the requirements from the day it takes effect` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE

§ `Reg 76.04 and 76.05 -- the reduction`

#ASSERT `reg 76.04 the employee's and employer's premiums payable under sections 67 and 68 of the Act are to be reduced` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.04 the employee's and employer's premiums payable under sections 67 and 68 of the Act are to be reduced` FALSE
-- 40,000 of insurable earnings and a reduction rate of 0.54%: 216.
#ASSERT `reg 76.05 the premium reduction obtained by applying the premium reduction rate` 40000 0.0054 EQUALS 216
#ASSERT `reg 76.05 the premium reduction obtained by applying the premium reduction rate` 40000 0 EQUALS 0

§ `Reg 76.06 -- the premium reduction rate`

-- Not covered: benefits 14,000, variable administrative costs 2,800, insurable earnings 100,000, self-employed earnings 40,000.
-- Divisor: 100,000 x 2.4 + 40,000 = 280,000, so 14,000/280,000 = 0.05 and 2,800/280,000 = 0.01 and (a) = 0.06.
`er4 test group not covered` MEANS `er4 Estimates for one group of persons` OF 14000, 2800, 100000, 40000
-- Covered: benefits 3,600, costs 600, insurable earnings 50,000, no self-employed earnings.
-- Divisor: 50,000 x 2.4 = 120,000, so 0.03 and 0.005 and (b) = 0.035.
`er4 test group covered` MEANS `er4 Estimates for one group of persons` OF 3600, 600, 50000, 0
-- A group with nothing to divide by.
`er4 test group with no earnings` MEANS `er4 Estimates for one group of persons` OF 1, 1, 0, 0

#ASSERT `reg 76.06(1) the sum of the estimated insurable earnings multiplied by 2.4 and the estimated self-employed earnings` `er4 test group not covered` EQUALS 280000
#ASSERT `reg 76.06(1) the sum of the estimated insurable earnings multiplied by 2.4 and the estimated self-employed earnings` `er4 test group covered` EQUALS 120000
#ASSERT `reg 76.06(1)(a)(i) and (b)(i) the result obtained by dividing the estimated benefits by the divisor` `er4 test group not covered` EQUALS JUST 0.05
#ASSERT `reg 76.06(1)(a)(ii) and (b)(ii) the result obtained by dividing the estimated variable administrative costs by the divisor` `er4 test group not covered` EQUALS JUST 0.01
#ASSERT `reg 76.06(1)(a) and (b) the rate determined by adding the two results` `er4 test group not covered` EQUALS JUST 0.06
#ASSERT `reg 76.06(1)(a)(i) and (b)(i) the result obtained by dividing the estimated benefits by the divisor` `er4 test group covered` EQUALS JUST 0.03
#ASSERT `reg 76.06(1)(a)(ii) and (b)(ii) the result obtained by dividing the estimated variable administrative costs by the divisor` `er4 test group covered` EQUALS JUST 0.005
#ASSERT `reg 76.06(1)(a) and (b) the rate determined by adding the two results` `er4 test group covered` EQUALS JUST 0.035
#ASSERT `reg 76.06(1)(a) and (b) the rate determined by adding the two results` `er4 test group with no earnings` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (a) minus (b): 0.06 - 0.035 = 0.025, already a whole number of hundredths of one per cent.
#ASSERT `reg 76.06(1) the premium reduction rate for a year` `er4 test group not covered` `er4 test group covered` EQUALS JUST 0.025
#ASSERT `reg 76.06(1) the premium reduction rate for a year` `er4 test group with no earnings` `er4 test group covered` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 76.06(1) the premium reduction rate for a year` `er4 test group not covered` `er4 test group with no earnings` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Rounding to one hundredth of one per cent (0.0001), the higher when equidistant: 0.02345 -> 0.0235; just below the
-- middle -> 0.0234; just above -> 0.0235.
#ASSERT `reg 76.06(1) the rate rounded to the nearest one hundredth of one per cent, as section 66.4 of the Act directs` 0.02345 EQUALS 0.0235
#ASSERT `reg 76.06(1) the rate rounded to the nearest one hundredth of one per cent, as section 66.4 of the Act directs` 0.023449 EQUALS 0.0234
#ASSERT `reg 76.06(1) the rate rounded to the nearest one hundredth of one per cent, as section 66.4 of the Act directs` 0.023451 EQUALS 0.0235
-- (2) and (3): only on actuarial estimates and having regard to the factors of section 66 of the Act.
#ASSERT `reg 76.06 the premium reduction rate determined as the regulation requires` TRUE TRUE `er4 test group not covered` `er4 test group covered` EQUALS JUST 0.025
#ASSERT `reg 76.06 the premium reduction rate determined as the regulation requires` FALSE TRUE `er4 test group not covered` `er4 test group covered` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 76.06 the premium reduction rate determined as the regulation requires` TRUE FALSE `er4 test group not covered` `er4 test group covered` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 76.06(2) actuarial estimates are used to determine the estimated amounts` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.06(2) actuarial estimates are used to determine the estimated amounts` FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 76.06(3) the results are determined having regard to the same factors as those set out in section 66 of the Act` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.06(3) the results are determined having regard to the same factors as those set out in section 66 of the Act` FALSE
